# CODEOWNERS — designated reviewers for security-sensitive paths (#910).
#
# GitHub requests a review from the listed owners automatically, and with
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled in branch protection, a PR that
# touches these paths cannot merge without an owner's approval.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the LAST matching rule wins. Keep broad
# rules first and narrow overrides below them. Never add a pattern without an
# owner here: a bare pattern REMOVES ownership from matching files.
#
# Coverage is enforced by `pnpm run governance:check`
# (scripts/validate-governance.mjs, SECURITY_SENSITIVE_PATHS). When you add a
# new wallet, auth, or crypto module outside the paths below, add it both here
# and to that list. See docs/contributing.md#code-owners.

